name":"3rd ed.","pagination":"xxxvi, 359 p. ;","source_records":["ia:gnosticreligion00jona","marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run03.mrc:169861173:1566","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part01.utf8:42527328:780","bwb:9780807058015","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-010.mrc:34313133:1041","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_025.bib.mrc:340235420:3738"],"title":"The gnostic religion","dewey_decimal_class":["273/.1"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 342-355) and index."},"number_of_pages":359,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lccn":["00060852"],"isbn_10":["0807058017"],"publish_date":"2001","publish_country":"mau","by_statement":"Hans Jonas.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL1728736W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"uris":["http://www.loc.gov/catdir/description/hm031/00060852.html"],"oclc_numbers":["44713051"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"'...All investigations of detail over the last half century have proved divergent rather than convergent, and leave us with a portrait of Gnosticism in which the absence of a unifying character seems to be the salient feature' - Hans Jonas, Preface, 1958. No modern writer that I am aware of has brought life to Gnosticism as Jonas has. While in no way neglecting historical or theological issues, Jonas didn't get bogged down in them: he insisted on revealing the existential import of Gnosticism. Indeed, at the end of this book he explores the commonalities of ancient Gnosticism and Heidegger's existentialism. What does it mean to feel one is in a cosmos in which God is alien or absent? Jonas provides a broad sweep of the conditions at the time Gnosticism developed at the beginning of the Christian era. His writing is that of a scholar but not targetted only to scholars... He writes: '... Gnosticism is actually a product of synceticsm [so ] each of these theories can be supported from the sources and none of them is satisfactory alone; but neither is the combination of all of them [supportable] which would make Gnosticism out to mere a mere mosaic of these elements and so miss its autonomous essence.' Yet nearly fifty years later some scholars look for a single source for Gnosticism while many are unable to find a suitably bounded definition. Jonas would not cage Gnosticism. Instead he asserts 'The gnostic movement - such as we must call it - was a widespread phenomena in the critical centuries indicated, feeding like Christianity on the impulses of a widely prevalent human situation, and therefore erupting in many places, many forms, and many languages.' Jonas discusses many Gnostic texts and themes...\" -- Amazon.com."},"latest_revision":14,"revision":14,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-12-31T12:53:47.699161"}}},"ISBN:9780895269645":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780895269645","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL8250832M/Science_Politics_and_Gnosticism","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL8250832M/Science_Politics_and_Gnosticism","details":{"identifiers":{"goodreads":["650322"],"librarything":["687130"]},"title":"Science Politics and Gnosticism","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL30332A","name":"Eric Voegelin"}],"publish_date":"June 1986","publishers":["Regnery Pub"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"weight":"5.6 ounces","isbn_13":["9780895269645"],"physical_format":"Paperback","isbn_10":["0895269643"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"subjects":["Ethics & Moral Philosophy","Political","Unassigned Title","Philosophy"],"physical_dimensions":"8.5 x 5.2 x 0.2 inches","source_records":["amazon:0895269643","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2026-07-08:C0-GLK-938"],"key":"/books/OL8250832M","works":[{"key":"/works/OL485323W"}],"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:C0-GLK-938"],"latest_revision":7,"revision":7,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T15:03:11.581851"},"last_mo